; Example of the DNS zone carriers-testkit builds and serves as the source of truth for a run.
;
; The harness generates fresh Ed25519 keys each run and fills in the DKIM/ARC "p=" values, so
; this file is illustrative — it shows the record shape the mock DNS answers. Everything is a
; single flat, root-origin zone (all names are FQDNs), which lets one authority cover both the
; author domain (example.com) and the list domain (lists.example.org). An SOA/NS for the root is
; required for the authority to be valid; the nameserver name is never actually resolved because
; the daemon and sink talk to the mock server directly.

$TTL 60
.                                   IN SOA  ns.mock.test. hostmaster.mock.test. 1 3600 600 86400 60
.                                   IN NS   ns.mock.test.

; --- Author domain (the message's From: domain) -----------------------------------------------
auth._domainkey.example.com.        IN TXT  "v=DKIM1; k=ed25519; p=<author public key>"
_dmarc.example.com.                 IN TXT  "v=DMARC1; p=reject; adkim=r; aspf=r"
example.com.                        IN TXT  "v=spf1 ip4:127.0.0.1 -all"
example.com.                        IN A    127.0.0.1

; --- List domain (carriers signs and ARC-seals as this domain) --------------------------------
dkim._domainkey.lists.example.org.  IN TXT  "v=DKIM1; k=ed25519; p=<list DKIM public key>"
arc._domainkey.lists.example.org.   IN TXT  "v=DKIM1; k=ed25519; p=<list ARC public key>"
_dmarc.lists.example.org.           IN TXT  "v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; adkim=r; aspf=r"
lists.example.org.                  IN TXT  "v=spf1 ip4:127.0.0.1 -all"
lists.example.org.                  IN A    127.0.0.1
